  "reviews": [
    {
      "id": 5964803341,
      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "body": "## Review — #36: Add a table with details about the test images\n\nCI all green. The PR is documentation-only (TEST_IMAGES.md) plus minor script hygiene. The table is a useful addition, but it contains **significant factual errors** in the \"Samples / Photometric\" and \"Compression\" columns that need correcting before merge.\n\n### Findings\n\n**Major — Photometric interpretation mislabeled as \"CMYK\"**\n\nEight images are labeled \"CMYK\" but none of them are CMYK (PI=5). Their actual PhotometricInterpretation tags (tag 262) are:\n\n| Image | Table says | Actual PI | Real color space |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `dscf0013.tif` | CMYK (3 samples) | 6 | YCbCr |\n| `quad-jpeg.tif` | CMYK (3 samples) | 6 | YCbCr |\n| `smallliz.tif` | CMYK (3 samples) | 6 | YCbCr |\n| `ycbcr-cat.tif` | CMYK (3 samples) | 6 | YCbCr |\n| `zackthecat.tif` | CMYK (3 samples) | 6 | YCbCr |\n| `off_l16.tif` | CMYK (1 sample) | 32844 | CIE L*a*b* |\n| `off_luv24.tif` | CMYK (3 samples) | 32845 | CIE L*u*v* |\n| `off_luv32.tif` | CMYK (3 samples) | 32845 | CIE L*u*v* |\n\nThere are **no actual CMYK (PI=5) images** in the test suite. The table should either label these correctly or note that no CMYK test images exist.\n\n**Major — Compression mislabeled**\n\n| Image | Table says | Actual compression code | Correct label |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `oxford.tif` | JPEG | 5 (LZW) | LZW |\n| `quad-lzw.tif` | JPEG | 5 (LZW) | LZW |\n| `quad-tile.tif` | JPEG | 5 (LZW) | LZW |\n| `strike.tif` | JPEG | 5 (LZW) | LZW |\n| `ycbcr-cat.tif` | JPEG | 5 (LZW) | LZW |\n| `quad-jpeg.tif` | Pixar | 7 (JPEG) | JPEG |\n| `smallliz.tif` | ZLIB | 6 (Old JPEG) | Old JPEG |\n| `zackthecat.tif` | ZLIB | 6 (Old JPEG) | Old JPEG |\n| `ladoga.tif` | LZW | 8 (Deflate) | Deflate |\n\n**Minor**\n- `strike.tif` is listed as \"RGB (4 samples)\" — the photometric is RGB (PI=2) with 4 samples (RGBA). This is acceptable but could note \"RGB + extra sample\" for clarity.\n- `text.tif` compression listed as \"32809\" (raw code) — inconsistent with other entries that use human-readable names. Consider \"Custom (32809)\" or similar.\n\n### How the agent should verify\n\nThe table should be generated from actual TIFF tag values, not from filenames or assumptions. The project's own `TiffImage` class can read the PhotometricInterpretation tag (0x0106) and Compression tag (0x0103) from each file. Alternatively, a one-liner with Python's Pillow (`im.tag.get(262)`, `im.tag.get(259)`) gives the raw values, which can then be mapped to names per the TIFF spec (PI 0=WhiteIsZero, 1=BlackIsZero, 2=RGB, 3=Palette, 5=CMYK, 6=YCbCr, 8=CIELab; compression 1=None, 5=LZW, 6=OldJPEG, 7=JPEG, 8=Deflate, 32773=PackBits).\n\n### Verdict\nNo code changes; CI green. The documentation table needs correction of at least the 8 \"CMYK\" mislabels and the compression mislabels before merge. The underlying test images and their support status are unaffected.",
