code) — inconsistent with other entries that use human-readable names. Consider \"Custom (32809)\" or similar.\n\n### How the agent should verify\n\nThe table should be generated from actual TIFF tag values, not from filenames or assumptions. The project's own `TiffImage` class can read the PhotometricInterpretation tag (0x0106) and Compression tag (0x0103) from each file. Alternatively, a one-liner with Python's Pillow (`im.tag.get(262)`, `im.tag.get(259)`) gives the raw values, which can then be mapped to names per the TIFF spec (PI 0=WhiteIsZero, 1=BlackIsZero, 2=RGB, 3=Palette, 5=CMYK, 6=YCbCr, 8=CIELab; compression 1=None, 5=LZW, 6=OldJPEG, 7=JPEG, 8=Deflate, 32773=PackBits).\n\n### Verdict\nNo code changes; CI green. The documentation table needs correction of at least the 8 \"CMYK\" mislabels and the compression mislabels before merge. The underlying test images and their support status are unaffected.",
